    {
      "id": "pfgqd3h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "INTRODUCTION TO LIGHT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Light behaves both as a wave and a particle, demonstrating dual nature in various optical phenomena.",
        "Reflection follows the principle that the angle of incidence equals the angle of reflection on a plane surface.",
        "Refraction occurs when light changes speed while traveling from one transparent medium to another.",
        "Spherical mirrors and lenses are categorized into concave and convex types based on their curvature and focusing behavior.",
        "Defects of vision such as Myopia and Hypermetropia are corrected using suitable concave and convex lenses.",
        "Dispersion splits white light into its constituent VIBGYOR colors, while scattering explains optical atmospheric phenomena."
      ],
      "id": "ui3tyjl"
    },
